WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:06.060
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, Amen.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:13.220
The reading from the Sinaxadion, for November 1st, on which we commemorate.

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:19.810
The Holy and Wonderworking on Mercenaries, Cosmas and Damien.

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:25.090
On the first of the month, we celebrate the memory of the Holy and Mercenaries and Wonder

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:29.330
Workers, Cosmas and Damien.

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:35.250
And Cosmas and Damien were brothers according to the flesh and came from the region of Ephesus

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:38.410
in the province of Asia.

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:44.090
Sometime after they were born, their father, a pagan of noble lineage, embraced the Christian

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:45.090
faith.

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:52.050
But his early death left the two children at the sole care of their devout mother, Thildota,

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:55.130
who had been a Christian since childhood.

00:00:55.130 --> 00:01:02.210
She made every effort to bring up her sons in Piety by her own virtuous example.

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:08.490
Cosmas and Damien were educated in the various branches of learning of their day.

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:15.090
But turned away before long, from all vain knowledge, to devote themselves to the art

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:22.730
of medicine, that they might free their neighbors from every sickness and infirmity.

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:28.330
Despite the apostles sent forth by Christ, they were given the power to cast out unclean

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:36.090
spirits and to heal all manner of sickness with no other remedy than their prayer.

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:41.730
Having freely received the grace of the Holy Spirit, these new apostles freely gave.

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:49.370
They tended the rich just as they did the poor and strangers as their own relatives, asking

00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:52.370
nothing in return.

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:58.050
Their charity was such that their care extended even to animals.

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:03.330
So closely did they link the preaching of the gospel of salvation to healing, that although

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:10.730
they were qualified in medical science, they used by way of remedy neither Lancet nor Plaster,

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:18.090
but only the life-giving name of Christ, so that the Savior himself was the physician, who

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:23.250
working in them, healed souls and bodies.

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:28.130
Patients made their way from all quarters to their dwelling, and each one found healing and

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:32.130
comfort according to the measure of his faith.

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:38.090
Saint Damien, the younger brother, was the first to fall asleep in peace, followed sometime

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:41.210
later by Saint Cosmas.

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:47.170
Later after, crowds of Christians came in a constant stream to the church built over

00:02:47.170 --> 00:02:52.490
their tomb, at a place called Firmann.

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:59.330
Their precious relics and their icon were an abundant source of healing for the sick, who were

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:06.170
allowed to spend several days in the church, surrounded by prayers and supplications.

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:13.490
No one left without obtaining either a cure or the strength to bear with patience and hope,

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:22.820
the illness permitted by God for the salvation of his soul, through the prayers of our holy

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:29.660
fathers, O Lord, Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us and save us.
